# Control Systems
We running this shit back fr A+ guaranteed




## Git branch procedure - please follow:

# Only the first time you work on this:

install platformIO extension on vscode
git clone repo-url

# Each time you start working, before you make any changes:

git checkout -b [branch name]

git pull origin main



# Work on code, then after you have made progress, push to your branch:

git add .

git commit -m "Add something"

git push origin [branch name]

# On GitHub (website), when changes have been reviewed and ONLY DURING A LAB:

Create a Pull Request → review → merge

# After PR is merged, on VS code to remove your local branch:

git checkout main

git pull origin main

git branch -d [branch name]    (to remove repo from local system)

# To List Local Branches in Your Repo and check you are on main (shown in green)

git branch

# FOR RESOLVING CONFLICTS LOCALLY

1. Checkout the branch you want to merge into

git checkout main


2. Pull latest changes:

git pull origin main

3. Fetch the branch with changes
git fetch origin BRANCH_NAME

4. Attempt the merge locally
git merge origin/BRANCH_NAME


You will likely see:

CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in path/to/file


5. Resolve the conflicts manually
Open the conflicting files in your code editor.

Look for conflict marker.


6. Mark conflicts as resolved
git add path/to/conflicted_file


Repeat for all files with conflicts.

7. Commit the merge and push
git commit
git push origin main
